      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: review incomplete because event evidence is access-restricted\n\nI verified the relevant work order and September’s Pending Close timestamp, but **cannot determine whether a cost event was created afterward** from the records I am authorized to read.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order | **WO-2025-09-004** — Cooler Plate Pack, Modine Racine |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 / PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00**, as stored; no timezone offset supplied |\n| Source transaction | Not verifiable |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes late | Not calculable without the event-created timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe accessible records contain work orders, cost periods, and Oracle’s policy excerpt, but **no cost-event rows**. Access to the supporting records was denied because they require the records-custodian role. I requested an authorized extract and escalated the blocker. Missing event rows in the accessible records are **not evidence that no event occurred**.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225**, states that transactions created after Pending Close—even for the current or a prior period—will not be processed until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue to process. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing.\n\nConsequently, the event’s type, creation timestamp, and recorded accounting status are necessary before concluding whether its treatment was consistent with Oracle policy.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_f0bc38e87b5b/audit-report.json`; the submitted report remains marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
